From e47942e6e960023c3d01be9748c42f0357804f21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephenuffugus <99242197+Stephenuffugus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 20:57:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Self-host the fonts instead of fetching them from Google
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every cold load sent the user's IP, User-Agent and Referer to
fonts.gstatic.com before anything rendered. That is a real disclosure for an
app that otherwise keeps everything on the device, and nobody agreed to it.

It also broke the app where it is most meant to work. Trackfit is for standing
in front of a layout with a box of track; a basement or a club hall is exactly
where a remote font request fails and the page renders in Times New Roman.

Latin subsets only — Fraunces, IBM Plex Mono 400/500, IBM Plex Sans variable.
152 kB for all four. Also removed the runtimeCaching rules that pointed at
fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com: they were dead once the links
went, but they would have quietly re-enabled the request the moment a
stylesheet referenced those hosts again. woff2 added to globPatterns so the
faces precache with everything else.

Verified in a real browser with request interception: zero external requests.
---
 apps/web/index.html                           |  24 +++++++++++++-----
 apps/web/public/fonts/fraunces.woff2          | Bin 0 -> 67304 bytes
 apps/web/public/fonts/ibm-plex-mono-400.woff2 | Bin 0 -> 14708 bytes
 apps/web/public/fonts/ibm-plex-mono-500.woff2 | Bin 0 -> 14888 bytes
 apps/web/public/fonts/ibm-plex-sans.woff2     | Bin 0 -> 45712 bytes
 apps/web/vite.config.ts                       |  21 ++++-----------
 6 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 apps/web/public/fonts/fraunces.woff2
 create mode 100644 apps/web/public/fonts/ibm-plex-mono-400.woff2
 create mode 100644 apps/web/public/fonts/ibm-plex-mono-500.woff2
 create mode 100644 apps/web/public/fonts/ibm-plex-sans.woff2

diff --git a/apps/web/index.html b/apps/web/index.html
index f311b27..edc441c 100644
--- a/apps/web/index.html
+++ b/apps/web/index.html
@@ -18,12 +18,24 @@
       name="description"
       content="Sectional track combination finder for model railroaders. Tell it what's in your box and the gap you're trying to fill — get every combination that fits, exactly or close."
     />
-    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
-    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
-    <link
-      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,500;9..144,700;9..144,900&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap"
-      rel="stylesheet"
-    />
+    <!-- Fonts are self-hosted, not fetched from Google.
+         Two reasons, and the first is the important one. A webfont request tells
+         fonts.gstatic.com the IP of everyone who opens Trackfit, on every cold
+         load — which is a real disclosure for an app that otherwise keeps its
+         data on the device, and it is not one the user ever agreed to. The
+         second is that the whole app is meant to work on a basement floor with
+         no signal, and a remote font is a request that fails there.
+         Latin subsets only, 152 kB for all four faces. -->
+    <style>
+      @font-face{font-family:'Fraunces';src:url('./fonts/fraunces.woff2') format('woff2');
+        font-weight:500 900;font-display:swap;font-style:normal}
+      @font-face{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono';src:url('./fonts/ibm-plex-mono-400.woff2') format('woff2');
+        font-weight:400;font-display:swap;font-style:normal}
+      @font-face{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono';src:url('./fonts/ibm-plex-mono-500.woff2') format('woff2');
+        font-weight:500;font-display:swap;font-style:normal}
+      @font-face{font-family:'IBM Plex Sans';src:url('./fonts/ibm-plex-sans.woff2') format('woff2');
+        font-weight:400 600;font-display:swap;font-style:normal}
+    </style>
   </head>
   <body>
     <div id="root"></div>
